			"widgets_values":[
				"Create a 10-second, 16:9, 3840x2160 ultra-detailed cinematic first-person POV racing video with epic blockbuster quality. The viewer is a professional MotoGP rider in the middle of an extreme high-speed race on a world-class circuit. The entire video is from the rider’s helmet perspective, showing the front fairing, handlebars, dashboard, mirrors, racing gloves, and the aggressive lean angle of the superbike during intense cornering and acceleration.\n\nThe scene begins already at very high speed on the main straight. The motorcycle engine roars with powerful, realistic mechanical detail. The rider is fully focused, gripping the handlebars tightly, rushing forward with explosive acceleration. Other racing motorcycles appear ahead and to the sides, with dynamic overtakes, rapid lane changes, and intense competitive pressure. The camera captures realistic helmet shake, wind pressure, vibration, and suspension feedback while maintaining a polished cinematic feel.\n\nFrom 0 to 3 seconds, the rider exits a corner aggressively and opens the throttle hard onto a straight, the engine screaming as the bike surges forward. The speed sensation is extreme, with fast-moving trackside barriers, blurred grandstands, flashing sponsor boards, sunlight reflections on the visor, and heat shimmer from the asphalt. From 3 to 7 seconds, the rider closes in on two competitors ahead, dives into a high-speed turn, leans dramatically with knee nearly scraping the ground, then overtakes one rider on corner exit in a bold maneuver. From 7 to 10 seconds, the rider accelerates into another straight, chasing the lead pack, with a final burst of speed, rising engine pitch, intense forward momentum, and a triumphant near-heroic racing climax.\n\nVisual style: photorealistic, high-end action cinema, dramatic lighting, rich contrast, realistic reflections, subtle motion blur, physically accurate track motion, cinematic depth, epic sports-film atmosphere, premium commercial quality, world-class motorsport broadcast feeling mixed with Hollywood action intensity. The race track should feel authentic, with curbs, asphalt texture, safety barriers, painted lines, spectators in the distance, and dynamic sky lighting. Emphasize speed, danger, precision, adrenaline, and immersion.\n\nAudio design: powerful high-revving superbike engine, rapid gear shifts, wind rushing past the helmet, tire grip sounds, subtle brake input sounds, track ambience, distant crowd energy, and race atmosphere. Add epic cinematic hybrid music with pounding percussion, rising orchestral brass, deep bass pulses, tension-building strings, and modern trailer-style energy. The music should start intense and keep building, matching the acceleration and overtakes, reaching a strong climax near the end.\n\nVoice and language: include a short, intense Chinese internal monologue / radio-style voiceover from the rider, synchronized naturally with the action, in a determined, adrenaline-filled tone. Suggested lines:\n“稳住，继续压！”\n“就是现在，超他！”\n“冲！再快一点！”\nThe voice should sound focused, fierce, and immersive, mixed naturally above the engine and music without overpowering them.\n\nKeep everything coherent and realistic. No third-person shots, no cutaways, no slow pacing, and no comedic tone. Maintain a continuous first-person racing perspective throughout the entire 10 seconds. No subtitles, no watermark, no logo overlay, no low-detail background, no distorted bike controls, and no unrealistic body motion. Prioritize intense immersion, cinematic realism, and epic racing spectacle.",
				1344,
				768,
				73
